  "question": {
    "text": "Two uniform brass rods A and B of lengths <math><mi>l</mi></math> and <math><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi></math> and radii <math><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi></math>and <math><mi>r</mi></math> respectively are heated to the same temperature. The ratio of the increase in the volumes of A to that of B is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3KiHR",
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FiL0T",
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "w9H69",
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "42vtD",
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For brass rod A<br /><br />Volume <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math>= <math><mi>&pi;</mi><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>&times;</mo><mi>l</mi></math> ...(i)<br /><br />For volume expansion<br /><br /><math><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msubsup> <mtext>V</mtext> <mn>1</mn> <mo>&prime;</mo> </msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&gamma;</mi><mo>∆</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&rArr;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><msubsup> <mtext>V</mtext> <mn>1</mn> <mo>&prime;</mo> </msubsup><mrow></mrow><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&prop;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br />Or <math><mo>∆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&prop;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> ...(ii)<br /><br />Similarly, for brass rod B<br /><br />Volume <math><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&pi;</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&times;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi></math> ...(iii)<br /><br />and <math><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>∆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>&prop;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> ...(iv)<br /><br />Dividing Eq. (i) by Eq. (ii), we get<br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&pi;</mi><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&pi;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />From eqs. (ii) and (iv),<br /><br /><math><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>∆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
